      "message": "From 3f8a5612f90e91c6acf0f22bb5fa67ad1ce1c1e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Vineeth Pillai \u003cvineethrp@google.com\u003e\nDate: Mon, 07 Jul 2025 07:47:13 -0400\nSubject: [PATCH] ANDROID: iommu/vt-d: force enable all iommu when pkvm is enabled.\n\nWhen pkvm is enabled, we need memory protection from devices and hence\nall iommus need to be enabled. Override kernel commandline and enable\nall iommus if pkvm is enabled.\n\nBug: 391542119\nUpstream-Task: 402758258\nTest: Build and Boot\n\nChange-Id: I51c9478dbb92b0a5961352450eccf467c5751d12\nSigned-off-by: Vineeth Pillai \u003cvineethrp@google.com\u003e\n---\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c\nindex 2cf50df..6248f435 100644\n--- a/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c\n+++ b/drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.c\n@@ -3270,7 +3270,12 @@ int __init intel_iommu_init(void)\n \tif (list_empty(\u0026dmar_satc_units))\n \t\tpr_info(\"No SATC found\\n\");\n \n-\tinit_no_remapping_devices();\n+\t/*\n+\t * Do not ignore any dmars if pkvm is enabled so as to\n+\t * guarantee memory protection from devices.\n+\t */\n+\tif (!pkvm_enabled())\n+\t\tinit_no_remapping_devices();\n \n \tret \u003d init_dmars();\n \tif (ret) {",
